        description:
          "Everything in this programme must only ever be practiced against systems you own or are explicitly authorised to test — the single most important rule in offensive security.",
        keyPoints: [
          "Always obtain written authorisation before testing any system you don't own (Rules of Engagement)",
          "Practice exclusively on lab environments: TryHackMe, HackTheBox, PortSwigger Academy, DVWA, VulnMachines",
          "Responsible disclosure: report vulnerabilities to the vendor/owner before any public disclosure",
          "Unauthorised access is illegal in most jurisdictions (e.g. Computer Misuse Act, CFAA) regardless of intent",
        ],
      },
    ],
  },

  // ============================================================
  // M2: Networking
